\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, as to Thy dear Cross we flee,
\par And plead to be forgiven,
\par So let Thy life our pattern be,
\par And form our souls for heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Help us, through good report and ill,
\par Our daily cross to bear;
\par Like Thee to do our Father's will,
\par Our brethrens's grief  to share.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let grace our selfishess expel,
\par Our earthliness refine,
\par And kindness in our bosoms dwell,
\par As free and true as Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If joy at shall at Thy bidding fly,
\par And grief's dark day come on,
\par We, in our turn, would meekly cry:
\par Father, Thy will be done!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Should friends misjudge, or foes defame,
\par Or brethren faithless prove,
\par Then, like Thine own, be all our aim
\par To conquer them by love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Kept peaceful in the midst of strife,
\par Forgiving and forgiven,
\par O may we live the pilgrim's life,
\par And follow Thee to heaven.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

